    "text": "GPT-6 Astra + Three.js = SVG logo deformer\n/goal prompt: \n\n/goal Build Brand Instrument: a polished browser-based 3D creative instrument closely matching the attached reference image. Work autonomously through implementation, real-browser inspection, critique and fixes. Aim for a reviewable result within 3.5 hours, with a requested upper time budget of 4 hours. Record start time and check elapsed time between iterations. Finish earlier if the acceptance criteria are met.\n\nFIRST\nInspect the reference and read project instructions. Verify that you can launch the app, interact with its browser and inspect actual screenshots. Save the available reference in the project for repeated comparison. If the reference or browser inspection is unavailable, report that immediately. Never invent visual verification.\n\nSCOPE\nOne excellent M sculpture, chrome material and refined interaction.\nUse TypeScript, React, Vite and Three.js. Prefer WebGPURenderer with TSL and tested WebGL2 fallback. Adapt implementation where necessary while preserving real 3D. Separate geometry, motion, rendering and UI. No model API is needed at runtime.\n\nVISUAL TARGET\nPreserve the reference's flowing M, dense parallel silver plates, substantial volume, clean bevels, narrow gaps, broad white studio reflections, dark reflected bands, soft grounding shadow, white background and restrained black Manrope typography. The sculpture dominates the viewport.\nImprove physical coherence and usability without redesigning the art direction. The reference is an artistic target, never a texture used to fake the product.\n\nGEOMETRY AND MOTION\nBuild volumetric plates with sufficient topology for local bending, driven by a controllable rig or guide curves. Dragging the right arm creates a smooth local fan/wave with anchored regions and coherent influence across neighboring plates.\nRelease restores the rest configuration with stable, frame-rate-independent damped dynamics. Preserve believable thickness and limit extreme deformation. Keep normals, shadows and pointer picking consistent with the deformed surface.\nNo screen-space displacement, flat-image warping, prerecorded hero video or screenshot stand-in.\n\nFUNCTIONS\nWorking drag/release, camera orbit to inspect depth, spread adjustment, stiffness/damping controls, Reset and PNG export.\nPrioritize this core. Arbitrary SVG import, audio and extra modes are later work. Show only functional controls.\n\nITERATION LOOP\nImplement a valuable change.\nRun the app and inspect real screenshots at consistent viewport/camera settings.\nExercise drag, release, reset and export.\nIdentify the three largest remaining visual or functional defects.\nFix the most important defect and repeat.\nSave useful checkpoints and comparison images. Preserve the best working version. If repeated changes fail, change the approach.\nA successful build alone does not mean completion.\n\nACCEPTANCE\nRecognizable sculptural M; crisp separated plates; convincing chrome; close reference composition.\nSmooth localized deformation and stable recovery without visible tearing or severe intersections.\nActual volume confirmed from another camera angle.\nWorking controls/export, no blocking console errors and successful build.\nInspect motion through video or timed frame sequences.\nMeasure performance in the available browser; report backend and hardware limitations. Aim for 60fps on desktop without claiming untested results.\nDo not weaken criteria or rely only on a self-assigned quality score.\n\nHANDOFF\nReserve the final 15 minutes for validation and handoff.\nPreserve source, lockfile, startup instructions, best screenshot, deformed/restored states, another camera angle and motion evidence.\nWrite REVIEW.md with completed checks, remaining visual gaps and next steps.\nAt the time budget or a genuine blocker, save the best result and report unmet criteria honestly. Do not idle to consume time.\nMake routine decisions independently within project permissions. Do not publish publicly, purchase services or modify unrelated projects.",
